<?php $experiment=$data['experiment']; ?>
<div class="page-actions"><?php badge($experiment['source']); ?><a class="button small" href="/exports/experiment/<?= e($experiment['id']) ?>.csv">Decisions CSV</a><a class="button small" href="/exports/experiment/<?= e($experiment['id']) ?>.pdf">PDF report</a><a class="underlined" href="/exports/experiment/<?= e($experiment['id']) ?>.json">Full reproducibility JSON</a></div>
<article class="panel spaced"><h2><?= e($experiment['name']) ?></h2><p>Dataset: <?= e($experiment['dataset_name']) ?> · Configuration: <?= e($experiment['version']) ?> · Outcome seed: <?= e($experiment['seed']) ?></p><p>Dataset SHA-256: <code><?= e($experiment['content_hash']) ?></code></p><p>All runs use the same eligibility checks, capacity budgets and latent outcome inputs. Earliest-deadline-first processes donation deadlines first, then selects the nearest eligible receiver. Other approaches process listing creation order. This is a snapshot allocation experiment; reserved capacity stays committed for the run.</p><details><summary>Dataset metadata and limitations</summary><pre><?= e(json_encode($experiment['metadata'],JSON_PRETTY_PRINT|JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE)) ?></pre></details><details><summary>Algorithm parameters</summary><pre><?= e(json_encode(['weights'=>$experiment['weights'],'parameters'=>$experiment['parameters']],JSON_PRETTY_PRINT)) ?></pre></details></article>
<article class="panel spaced"><h2>Recorded comparison</h2><button type="button" class="quiet-button" data-download-chart>Download comparison chart (PNG)</button><div class="chart-wrap"><canvas data-chart="bar" data-labels="<?= e(json_encode(array_column($experiment['runs'],'algorithm'))) ?>" data-values="<?= e(json_encode(array_map(fn($run)=>$run['metrics']['pickup_success_rate']!==null ? $run['metrics']['pickup_success_rate']*100 : null,$experiment['runs']))) ?>" data-series="Simulated pickup success (%)" aria-label="Algorithm comparison chart"></canvas></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><?php foreach ($experiment['runs'] as $run): ?><th><?= e($run['algorithm']) ?></th><?php endforeach ?></tr></thead><tbody><?php $first=$experiment['runs'][0] ?? null;if ($first):foreach (array_keys($first['metrics']) as $metric): ?><tr><th><?= e(str_replace('_',' ',$metric)) ?></th><?php foreach ($experiment['runs'] as $run): ?><td><?= $run['metrics'][$metric]!==null ? e(number_format($run['metrics'][$metric],4)) : 'N/A' ?></td><?php endforeach ?></tr><?php endforeach;endif ?><tr><th>Execution time (ms)</th><?php foreach ($experiment['runs'] as $run): ?><td><?= e($run['execution_ms']) ?></td><?php endforeach ?></tr></tbody></table></div></article>
<article class="panel spaced"><h2>Metric definitions and interpretation</h2><p>Pickup success = completed / accepted assignments. Expired or uncollected rate = eligible donations not successfully collected / eligible listings, including failed and unassigned records. Distance averages successful pickups only. Capacity utilization = assigned kg / total capacity budget. Matching time is total algorithm runtime / eligible listings.</p><p>Prediction classification uses feasibility score ≥ 0.25 as a positive prediction. Precision, recall, F1 and ROC-AUC are undefined where their denominators or class pairs are absent. The feasibility score is not a calibrated probability, so a Brier score is not reported. Timing measurements vary by execution; seeded decisions and outcome metrics are reproducible.</p><p>This implementation uses simulated outcomes for all scenario sources; importing pilot inputs does not turn simulated outcomes into observed pilot results. TAMRA is a proposed method, with no claim of novelty or superiority.</p></article>

<article class="panel spaced"><h2>Repeated-run summary for this dataset and configuration</h2><p>Run another comparison with a different outcome seed to assess variability. Repeated identical seeds reproduce outcomes and do not provide independent evidence.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Algorithm</th><th>Runs / distinct seeds</th><th>Mean pickup success rate</th><th>Sample standard deviation</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach ($experiment['replicate_summary'] as $summary):$stat=$summary['metrics']['pickup_success_rate'] ?? null; ?><tr><td><?= e($summary['algorithm']) ?></td><td><?= e($summary['runs']) ?> / <?= e($summary['distinct_seeds']) ?></td><td><?= $stat ? e(number_format($stat['mean'],4)) : 'N/A' ?></td><td><?= $stat && $stat['sample_stddev']!==null ? e(number_format($stat['sample_stddev'],4)) : 'N/A — one run' ?></td></tr><?php endforeach ?></tbody></table></div></article>
